/**
@page cosmology_numerics Discrete initialization, force and time integration

@section numerics_fourier Fourier normalization and placement

For an N^3 mesh the IPPL transform pair is
@f[ \widehat u_{\boldsymbol n}=N^{-3}\sum_{\boldsymbol j}u_{\boldsymbol j}
 e^{-2\pi i\boldsymbol n\cdot\boldsymbol j/N},\qquad
u_{\boldsymbol j}=\sum_{\boldsymbol n}\widehat u_{\boldsymbol n}
 e^{+2\pi i\boldsymbol n\cdot\boldsymbol j/N}. @f]
Physical wavenumbers are @f$\boldsymbol k=2\pi\boldsymbol n/L@f$. Particles
start at @f$\boldsymbol q=(\boldsymbol j+1/2)L/N@f$. Initial coefficients include
@f$\exp[i\pi(n_x+n_y+n_z)/N]@f$, the half-cell evaluation phase. Global particle
IDs are x-fast. Do not change Fourier normalization or centering independently
of coefficient variance, force kernels or reference coordinate shifts.

@section numerics_ic Initial conditions

Production Gaussian coefficients satisfy
@f[ \mathbb E[|\widehat\delta_{\boldsymbol n}|^2]=P_0(k)/L^3,\quad
\widehat\delta_{-\boldsymbol n}=\widehat\delta_{\boldsymbol n}^{*}. @f]
A canonical conjugate-pair mesh index, the configured uint64 seed and SplitMix64
finalization define independent open-interval variates. For @f$u_1,u_2\in(0,1)@f$,
@f[ \widehat\delta=\sqrt{-\ln u_1\,P_0(k)/L^3}
 [\cos(2\pi u_2)+i\sin(2\pi u_2)]. @f]
Conjugation flips the imaginary sign for the other member. DC and every
componentwise IC Nyquist plane are zero. Coefficients are independent of MPI
ownership and kernel scheduling at a fixed mesh size. The key contains the
mesh index and N: it is not a promise of common phases across different meshes.

The shared Python Gaussian fixture instead hashes a physical integer mode and
seed with SHA256, then applies Box-Muller. This continuous-mode contract supplies
common phases across particle/force-mesh refinements. It deliberately differs
from production SplitMix64. The standard fixture API caps its band at 12;
the three-code campaign explicitly constructs the larger band through 48.
Cross-code initial conditions are shared CSVs, not an assumption that different
RNG implementations produce identical states from the same seed.

Zel'dovich/1LPT @cite zeldovich1970 uses
@f[ \widehat{\boldsymbol\psi}_0(\boldsymbol k)
= i\boldsymbol k\widehat\delta(\boldsymbol k)/k^2,\qquad
\boldsymbol x=\operatorname{wrap}(\boldsymbol q+D\boldsymbol\psi_0),\quad
\boldsymbol p=a^2E(a)f(a)D(a)\boldsymbol\psi_0. @f]
For sine inputs the supplied amplitude is delta at the initial redshift, so the
coefficient is divided by D(aInitial) before this displacement step. Uniform
inputs have zero perturbation and canonical momentum. Python shared fixtures
round canonical momenta once to float32 and return those values as float64;
this matches the native reference's particle storage, not a production IPPL
precision restriction. Sampled positive initial-map Jacobians are an initial
sanity check, not proof of global injectivity.

@section numerics_cic Particle-mesh gravity

CIC uses the tensor-product triangular assignment kernel
@f[ S(\boldsymbol u)=\prod_{d=1}^3\max(0,1-|u_d|). @f]
Mass is scattered to neighboring periodic mesh sites, the density contrast is
formed, and the same assignment kernel gathers mesh forces to particles.
For unequal imported particle/mesh loads the unit-weight mean cell mass is
@f$\bar m=N_P^3/N_M^3@f$ and @f$\delta_i=m_i/\bar m-1@f$.
For the production one-particle-per-cell load this reduces to @f$\delta_i=m_i-1@f$.

The force component implemented by the spectral solve is
@f[ \widehat F_{0,j}(\boldsymbol k)=
\frac{3\Omega_m}{2}\frac{i\widetilde k_j}{|\boldsymbol k|^2}
\widehat\delta(\boldsymbol k). @f]
At DC it is zero. On the j-th Nyquist plane only @f$\widetilde k_j@f$ is zero;
the full denominator retains all squared components. This produces a real
discrete differentiated component without suppressing unrelated transverse
components. Native FastPM retains its own R2C convention: only its eight
self-conjugate corners are nulled by its native operator. Frozen-force tests
compare each solver with its own oracle and separately predict their difference.

There is no CIC deconvolution, extra softening kernel or short-range tree in
IPPL's force solve. Two assignment operations suppress short wavelengths;
continuum linear growth must therefore be assessed on resolved scales and under
refinement. The CIC-window corrections described in @ref cosmology_spectra are
measurement operations, never inserted into this production force kernel.

@section numerics_kdk Scale-factor kick-drift-kick

For endpoints a0,a1 and geometric midpoint @f$a_h=\sqrt{a_0a_1}@f$:
@f[ K(a,b)=\int_a^b\frac{da'}{a'^2E(a')},\qquad
R(a,b)=\int_a^b\frac{da'}{a'^3E(a')}. @f]
@f[ \boldsymbol p_h=\boldsymbol p_0+K(a_0,a_h)\boldsymbol F_0(\boldsymbol x_0),
\quad\boldsymbol x_1=\operatorname{wrap}[\boldsymbol x_0+R(a_0,a_1)\boldsymbol p_h], @f]
@f[ \boldsymbol p_1=\boldsymbol p_h+K(a_h,a_1)\boldsymbol F_0(\boldsymbol x_1). @f]
The new force is calculated after migration. Positions and momenta are
synchronized after the second kick. Endpoints obey
@f$a_i=a_{\rm in}\exp[i\ln(a_{\rm fin}/a_{\rm in})/N_t]@f$.
The host quadrature evaluates K and R in log(a). Reversed intervals return the
negative integral and equal endpoints return zero. In Einstein-de Sitter,
@f[ K(a,b)=2(\sqrt b-\sqrt a),\qquad
R(a,b)=2(a^{-1/2}-b^{-1/2}). @f]
This is the production second-order time scheme; it is not FastPM's modified
large-step prescription @cite feng2016fastpm or COLA @cite tassev2013cola.
The native evolution harness selects FASTPM_FORCE_PM explicitly.
Mechanical energy is not constant in an expanding background. Spatial
convergence, timestep convergence and decomposition reproducibility are
separate properties; no one of these substitutes for the others.

@section numerics_periodic Periodic ownership

Before every particle ownership update,
@f$x_d\leftarrow x_d-L\lfloor x_d/L\rfloor@f$ wraps finite overshoots spanning
multiple boxes. A result rounded to exactly L is reset to zero. The particle
container's boundary functor is disabled because this wrapper supplies the
periodicity; field layouts remain periodic. IDs, Lagrangian positions, mass,
force and momentum migrate together. No dynamic load-balancer hierarchy from
the removed historical StructureFormation implementation is used.

@section numerics_native_mode_hash Resolution-independent native 1LPT

For `ic_rng=mode_hash_v1`, an integer physical mode @f$\boldsymbol m@f$ is
canonical when its first nonzero Cartesian component is positive. Hash the exact
bytes `IPPL-band-limited-Gaussian-v1\0` followed by little-endian uint64 seed and
three little-endian signed int32 canonical components with SHA256. Interpret
bytes 0..7 and 8..15 as little-endian uint64 values, shift right by 12, then set
@f$u_j=(b_j+1/2)/2^{52}@f$. The canonical Gaussian coefficient is
@f$G=\sqrt{-\ln u_1}\exp(2\pi i u_2)@f$; its partner is the complex conjugate.
Thus @f$\langle|G|^2\rangle=1@f$, and
@f$\delta_{0,\boldsymbol m}=\sqrt{P_0(k)/L^3}G@f$.
This protocol has no mesh dimension, rank, traversal order or backend in its key.
Transcendental/FFT rounding is backend dependent; integer digest bits are exact.
The legacy branch retains the previous index-keyed realizations.

A positive `ic_mode_cutoff=M` retains @f$0<|\boldsymbol m|\le M<N/2@f$.
Neither the model normalization nor realization amplitude is readjusted after
truncation. Increasing N therefore samples the same continuous band-limited
field when seed, box, spectrum and cutoff agree. DC and Nyquist planes vanish.
Cell-centred FFT coefficients include @f$\exp(i\pi\sum_d m_d/N)@f$; removing that
sampling phase gives the same physical coefficient across resolutions.

The existing distributed inverse FFT yields @f$\boldsymbol\psi_0@f$ and then
@f$\boldsymbol x=\boldsymbol q+D(a_i)\boldsymbol\psi_0@f$,
@f$\boldsymbol p=a_i^2 E(a_i)f(a_i)D(a_i)\boldsymbol\psi_0@f$.
`ic_momentum_precision=float32` rounds the last expression once and widens it
back to double solely for compatibility with saved Python ICs. Default double
retains the original native arithmetic. No Poisson solver or KDK update changes.

The initializer runs in Kokkos execution memory and generates each local lattice
piece directly on its owning rank. Only the small radial spectrum table moves
host-to-device; no full particle IC file or host mesh is required. Scalar and
small-shell reductions in the automatic startup gate add communication but do
not alter particles, Fourier coefficients or subsequent force arithmetic.
The gate checks deterministic identities before evolution; realization scatter
in Gaussian shell powers is reported without rejecting or selecting seeds.
`pk_initial.csv` is the linear density spectrum associated with the displacement,
not a nonlinear particle/CIC spectrum and has no Poisson noise subtraction.

*/
